  "content": {
    "id": "p9-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "There are four red tokens and three blue tokens in a bag. Three tokens are removed at random without replacement. Find the probability of obtaining:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p9-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "at least one red token",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{34}{35}$",
          "worked": "The complement is drawing three blue tokens.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(\\text{at least one red})&=1-\\frac{3}{7}\\times\\frac{2}{6}\\times\\frac{1}{5}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{at least one red})&=1-\\frac{1}{35}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{at least one red})&=\\frac{34}{35}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "at least one blue token",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{31}{35}$",
          "worked": "The complement is drawing three red tokens.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(\\text{at least one blue})&=1-\\frac{4}{7}\\times\\frac{3}{6}\\times\\frac{2}{5}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{at least one blue})&=1-\\frac{4}{35}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{at least one blue})&=\\frac{31}{35}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "at least one token of each colour.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{6}{7}$\n\nSubtract the probabilities of three red tokens and three blue tokens from 1.",
          "worked": "The complement is drawing three red tokens or three blue tokens. These events are mutually exclusive.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(\\text{both colours})&=1-\\frac{4}{7}\\times\\frac{3}{6}\\times\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{3}{7}\\times\\frac{2}{6}\\times\\frac{1}{5}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{both colours})&=1-\\frac{4}{35}-\\frac{1}{35}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{both colours})&=\\frac{6}{7}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      }
    ]
  },
